## Stack
- Backend: Jac language. ALL agent logic in .jac files.
- Frontend: React + Vite + TypeScript + Tailwind CSS v4 + shadcn/ui
- LLM: Claude via byLLM (import:py from byllm.lib { Model })
- Real-time: WebSocket walker for agent step streaming
- No auth, no login, single demo user

## Critical Jac Syntax Rules
- Semicolons REQUIRED at end of every statement
- `has` for field declarations (never __init__)
- `can` for walker abilities with entry/exit triggers ONLY
- `def` for utility methods not tied to graph traversal
- `here` = current node being visited
- `self` = walker instance
- NEVER use `let` keyword (removed from Jac)
- NEVER use `check` keyword (removed from Jac)
- `++>` creates a new directed edge AND connects in one step
- `-->` traverses an EXISTING edge (does NOT create)
- `+>:EdgeType:+>` creates a typed directed edge
- `->:EdgeType:->` traverses a typed edge
- `[root-->][?:NodeType]` filters by node type
- `[root-->][?:NodeType, field == value]` filters by type + field
- `&jid_string` dereferences a JID back to a node object
- `jid(node)` returns the unique string ID of a node
- All nodes connected to root via ++> are auto-persisted
- `:pub` walkers become POST /walker/<WalkerName> endpoints
- byLLM: `result = ability() by llm()` NOT `method="ReAct"`
- Tools activate ReAct automatically: `by llm(tools=[...])`
- NEVER use method="ReAct" — it is deprecated and broken

## jac-scale Response Envelope (CRITICAL)
The actual response format is:
{ "status": 200, "reports": [...] }
NOT { "ok": true, "data": { "reports": [...] } }
Frontend reads: response.reports[0] NOT response.data.reports[0]

## Edge Syntax (UPDATED 2025)
# Create typed edge:
node_a +>:EdgeType:+> node_b;
# Traverse typed edge:
results = [here->:EdgeType:->][?:NodeType];
# Create untyped edge:
root ++> new_node;
# Traverse untyped:
all = [root-->][?:NodeType];

## CORS
jac-scale default mode allows ALL origins automatically.
No CORS configuration needed. Use Vite proxy for clean URLs.

